      "Broad-sense heritability is defined as the proportion of phenotypic variance attributable to ALL genetic variation in the population: $H^2 = \\text{Var}(G) / V_P$. But here, $G$ is not just the direct effect! If parental genotypes causally influence phenotype, parental genetic variance IS part of the genetic architecture, or if $H^2$ is defined as direct genotypic variance, look at what $V_P$ contains: $V_P = V_A(1 + c + 0.5 c^2) + V_e$.",
